{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Seven days it shall be with its mother.</b> This is a warning to the priest — that if he comes to hasten his offering, he must not hasten before eight days, for it lacks its time." "<b>On the eighth day you shall give it to Me.</b> Might one think it is obligatory to give it by day? 'Eighth' is stated here and 'from the eighth day onward it shall be accepted' is stated below (Leviticus 22) — just as 'eighth' stated below serves to make fit from the eighth day onward, so too 'eighth' stated here serves to make fit from the eighth day onward; and so its sense: on the eighth day you are permitted to give it to Me (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:00.453410116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}